## 7. Feature-Level Target State

The marketplace should behave like a governed supply-chain registry. Plugin versions should be immutable signed artifacts with digest, provenance, SBOM, vulnerability, malware, and license scan state. Install policy should be environment-scoped and fail closed. Approved installs should generate runtime tool/capability policy grants and revoke them on disable/uninstall/revocation. UI should expose evidence, risk, policy, install status, and lifecycle controls. Tests should prove signature verification, scan gates, install policy, runtime grant enforcement, lifecycle cascade, and frontend/backend contract consistency.

